Subject: bluetooth: sync legacy advertising state on peripheral connect

The controller leaves the legacy Advertising State when a peripheral
connection is established. Clear the host advertising cache on a successful
peripheral LE connection, before allocating the connection object, so an
allocation failure cannot leave the cache stale. Central connections and
failed connection events do not change this state.

Treat a stop request as successful when the host cache already records
advertising as disabled. This avoids sending a redundant controller command
after a peripheral connection while preserving allocation and command errors
for an active stop.

The state transition follows the Bluetooth Core Link Layer Advertising State
rules for connection establishment.
https://www.bluetooth.com/wp-content/uploads/Files/Specification/HTML/Core-54/out/en/low-energy-controller/link-layer-specification.html

--- a/wireless/bluetooth/bt_hcicore.c
+++ b/wireless/bluetooth/bt_hcicore.c
@@ -720,6 +720,16 @@
   wlinfo("status %u handle %u role %u %s\n", evt->status, handle,
          evt->role, bt_addr_le_str(&evt->peer_addr));
 
+  /* A successful peripheral connection stops legacy advertising in the
+   * controller. Keep the host cache in sync before connection allocation,
+   * which can fail independently of the completed link.
+   */
+
+  if (evt->status == 0 && evt->role == BT_HCI_ROLE_SLAVE)
+    {
+      g_btdev.adv_enable = 0;
+    }
+
   /* Make lookup to check if there's a connection object in CONNECT state
    * associated with passed peer LE address.
    */
@@ -2411,8 +2421,8 @@
 
   if (!g_btdev.adv_enable)
     {
-      wlwarn("WARNING:  Already advertising\n");
-      return -EALREADY;
+      wlinfo("Advertising already stopped\n");
+      return 0;
     }
 
   buf = bt_hci_cmd_create(BT_HCI_OP_LE_SET_ADV_ENABLE, 1);
